# No CIF or Margin Data in Client-Facing Documents

## Rule

**NEVER include CIF prices, supplier buy prices, margin percentages, or installed cost breakdowns in any client-facing document.**

CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) is Lighthief's purchase price from Linyang. Exposing it reveals the margin structure and undermines commercial positioning.

## What to NEVER show clients

- CIF values (e.g. "CIF: €1,848,712" or "CIF €92.14/kWh")
- Installed cost breakdowns (CIF + adders = installed)
- Margin amounts or percentages (e.g. "margin: 12.46%")
- Adder line items with costs (import duty amounts, transport costs, etc.)
- Any reference to `portfolio-data.ts` fields: `cif`, `installedCost`, `margin`, `marginPct`

## What IS safe to show clients

- Final EPC turnkey price (e.g. "€2,258,900")
- Price per kWh/MWh (e.g. "€112,945/MWh")
- Payment milestone amounts (30/55/10/5 of EPC price)
- EMS/SCADA capex and annual fees (client-paid items)
- Extended warranty rates (client pays Linyang directly)
- LTSA O&M rates (€1,740/MWh/yr)
- "CIF Limassol" as an incoterms/shipping term (not as a price)

## Where CIF data belongs

- `lib/portfolio-data.ts` (SSOT, internal only)
- `docs/internal/` documents (internal analysis)
- `scripts/adders_output.txt` (internal calculations)
- `docs/quotations/` (supplier quotations, internal)

## If you find CIF in a client doc

Remove the CIF row/value immediately. Replace with the client-facing EPC price or €/kWh rate only.
